{"id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:kth-order-pde","title":"def:kth-order-pde","path":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.md","line":10,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.tex#def:kth-order-pde","uses":[],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.tex","label":"def:kth-order-pde","line":11,"source":"\\begin{definition}[$k$th-Order Partial Differential Equation]\n\\label{def:kth-order-pde}\n\n\n\\dcref{ch1:1.1-def-1}\n\\group{PDE Basics}\n\n\nFix an integer $k \\geq 1$ and an open set $U \\subseteq \\R^n$. Given\n$$F : \\R^{n^k} \\times \\R^{n^{k-1}} \\times \\cdots \\times \\R^n \\times \\R \\times U \\to \\R,$$\nand an unknown $u : U \\to \\R$, an equation\n\\begin{equation}\nF(D^k u(x), D^{k-1} u(x), \\ldots, Du(x), u(x), x) = 0 \\qquad (x \\in U)\n\\tag{1}\n\\end{equation}\nis a $k$th-order partial differential equation (PDE).\n\\end{definition}\n\nA solution satisfies (1), possibly subject to auxiliary boundary conditions on\na subset $\\Gamma$ of $\\partial U$.","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[<span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$k$\">$k$</span>th-Order Partial Differential Equation] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a6b74682d6f726465722d706465\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch1:1.1-def-1</span></span>\\group PDE Basics <p></p>Fix an integer <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$k \\geq 1$\">$k \\geq 1$</span> and an open set <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$U \\subseteq \\R ^n$\">$U \\subseteq \\R ^n$</span>. Given <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[ F : \\R ^{n^k} \\times \\R ^{n^{k-1}} \\times \\cdots \\times \\R ^n \\times \\R \\times U \\to \\R , \\]\">\\[ F : \\R ^{n^k} \\times \\R ^{n^{k-1}} \\times \\cdots \\times \\R ^n \\times \\R \\times U \\to \\R , \\]</span> and an unknown <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u : U \\to \\R $\">$u : U \\to \\R $</span>, an equation <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\begin{equation}  F(D^k u(x), D^{k-1} u(x), \\ldots , Du(x), u(x), x) = 0 \\qquad (x \\in U) \\tag {1} \\end{equation}\">\\begin{equation}  F(D^k u(x), D^{k-1} u(x), \\ldots , Du(x), u(x), x) = 0 \\qquad (x \\in U) \\tag {1} \\end{equation}</span> is a <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$k$\">$k$</span>th-order partial differential equation (PDE).  <p></p>A solution satisfies (1), possibly subject to auxiliary boundary conditions on a subset <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Gamma $\">$\\Gamma $</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\partial U$\">$\\partial U$</span>.","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: group"]},"previous":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#sec:pde-introduction","next":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:linear-semilinear-quasilinear-fully-nonlinear","relations":[],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:linear-semilinear-quasilinear-fully-nonlinear","title":"def:linear-semilinear-quasilinear-fully-nonlinear","label":"def:linear-semilinear-quasilinear-fully-nonlinear"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#def:kth-order-system-pde","title":"def:kth-order-system-pde","label":"def:kth-order-system-pde"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#ex:laplaces-equation","title":"ex:laplaces-equation","label":"ex:laplaces-equation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#ex:helmholtz-eigenvalue-equation","title":"ex:hel